export anchor RoadTripStyle:
    number: 418
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Road trip
    idea: The trip as a car instrument cluster at night, a budget gauge and a checklist gauge with orange needles flanking a cyan navigation screen, warning style lights for the checklist, and the itinerary read out as turn by turn route guidance.
    base: dark
    palette:
        road: #06080a, the page and the style sheet
        cluster: #0d1114, the cluster hood, the guidance panel and list rows
        face: #12171b, gauge faces
        rim: #2a3238, gauge rims and the cluster edge
        line: #24303a, row rules and empty gauge arcs
        ink: #eaf2f5, text and figures
        muted: #9fb0b8, labels, ticks and captions
        needle: #ff6a3d, gauge needles, the logo and the primary button
        cyan: #5ee6ff, the nav route, gauge fill, Flight rows and focus
        go: #6ee07a, Booked and Done lights
        caution: #ffbf3c, Not booked, To do and the next to book line
    type:
        Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, Arial.
        Base 16px at 1.45. Gauge figures 30px tabular, the trip title 30px
        at 600, section titles 22px caps at 600, dates 20px at 600 tabular,
        labels 12px caps tracked 0.12em in muted.
    layout:
        A top bar with an orange outlined B and Brightwork Trips in small
        caps on the left, Japan in April centred, and the dates and Mara
        Okafor and one guest on the right. Below sits the cluster, a wide
        hood with an arched top and a 2px rim, shaded dark inside. Three
        parts sit in it. On the left a round Budget gauge, a 240 degree
        scale from 0 to 5,000 with a cyan arc filled to 3,200 and an orange
        needle, reading 3,200 euro saved and 1,800 to go. In the middle a
        cyan navigation screen with Next to book Train to Kyoto 6 Apr in
        caution yellow, a route on a grid from Tokyo to Kyoto to Osaka with
        ringed nodes and an orange position mark, and readouts Trip 14 days,
        Outside Tokyo early April 17 degrees high and Cherry blossom likely.
        On the right a Checklist gauge from 0 to 4 with the needle at 2.
        Under a rule four warning lights show each check with a check circle
        and Done or a caution triangle and To do. Below the cluster, Route
        guidance lists six legs, each with a rounded icon tile, a big date,
        the leg and detail and a status. Two buttons end the panel. Below
        900px the nav screen moves above the gauges and at phone width the
        gauges stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 36px cluster padding, 16px between gauges and screen and 12px guidance rows.
    density: Medium. Two gauges, a nav screen and four lights in the cluster, six guidance rows below.
    corners: An arched hood with a 220 by 140px top radius, a 14px screen, 12px icon tiles, 8px lights and 10px buttons.
    borders: A 2px rim on the hood and gauge faces and 1px rules between guidance rows.
    shadows: Deep inset shade at the top of the hood and a soft cyan halo round gauges and focus.
    icons:
        2px line icons in rounded tiles. Booked and Done are a check circle,
        Not booked and To do a caution triangle and Flight a plane, always
        beside the word.
    focus: A 3px cyan outline offset 3px with a cyan glow.
    tone: Driver prompts such as Next to book, Route guidance and Outside.
